==Strategy==
This stage introduces Darkmadillo, a non-[[:Category:Sage Enemies|Sage]], original enemy who is essentially a much smaller [[Tackey]], being designed to punish mistimed units. One Darkmadillo is usually fairly easy to take care of, but letting them stack can quickly result in danger. Darkmadillo's health makes it decently squishy, yet pretty annoying to fully kill given its two Knockbacks and tendancy to stay behind the frontline, meaning the best way to kill it is to first use high-damage units like [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]], then use methods of pierce like [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]]'s Wave or [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]] to kill it.

In this stage in particular, your weapon of choice to snipe Darkmadillo will probably be [[Dom Cat (Special Cat)|Dark Lazer]]'s Wave Attacks given that everything but Celeboodle is Red or Black, meaning Lazer's Waves will be able to continuously stack on Dark Dober and snipe the Darkmadillos. Note that because Raynard spawns on base hit, you can use [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] to have him hit the base, and then either leave Raynard with almost no health or use an small Attack [[Cat Combo|Combo]] to just kill him outright. Once that happens, the only enemies present here will be frontline enemies like Doctor K.O and Ragin' Gory, who are both Dark Lazer fodder.

